@startuml
!theme cyborg
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam defaultFontColor #F3F4F6
skinparam ArrowColor #CBD5E1
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #164E63
skinparam ArrowColor #164E63
skinparam sequence {
 ParticipantBackgroundColor #164E63
 ParticipantBorderColor #164E63
 ParticipantFontColor #164E63
 ActorBorderColor #164E63
 ActorFontColor #164E63
 LifeLineBorderColor #164E63
 LifeLineBackgroundColor #111827
 GroupBackgroundColor #164E63
 GroupBodyBackgroundColor #111827
 GroupBorderColor #164E63
 GroupHeaderFontColor #164E63
 GroupFontColor #164E63
 ArrowColor #164E63
 ArrowFontColor #164E63
 DividerBackgroundColor #164E63
 DividerBorderColor #164E63
 DividerFontColor #164E63
}
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #164E63
skinparam noteBorderColor #164E63
skinparam noteFontColor #164E63
skinparam shadowing false
title Scoped Core / ProjectForge Interaction
actor "Invited user" as user
participant "Core application" as core #164E63
participant "ProjectForge API" as forge #164E63
participant "Core entitlement endpoint" as status #164E63
database "ProjectForge owned records" as store
user -> core : Request permitted repository operation
core -> core : Validate local session and input
core -> forge : Authenticated scoped actor request\nWrite identity/version where applicable
forge -> forge : Validate caller, token and scope
alt Invalid identity / scope
 forge --> core : Contract-defined denial; no business effect
else Caller context valid
 forge -> status : Narrow status-only entitlement request
 alt Required authority unavailable
  status --> forge : No usable authority result
  forge --> core : 503 unavailable; no protected operation
 else Current status resolved
  status --> forge : Current account / entitlement status
  forge -> forge : Check entitlement and local resource/action grant
  alt Actor or action not authorized
   forge --> core : Contract-defined denial; no business effect
  else Authorized
   forge -> store : Validate version / request identity\nRead or perform owning local transaction
   store --> forge : Recorded result or conflict
   forge --> core : Permitted result / stable error + correlation ID
  end
 end
end
core --> user : Accurate success, denial, conflict or unavailable outcome
note over core, forge
A lost response does not establish remote rollback.
Resolve recorded request identity before an unsafe repeat.
end note
@enduml
